<script type="application/json">{"nodes": [{"id": "table", "label": "Users table"}, {"id": "query", "label": "Observable query"}, {"id": "ui", "label": "Collector"}], "layouts": {"wide": {"size": [760, 260], "nodes": {"table": {"x": 24, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}, "query": {"x": 276, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}, "ui": {"x": 528, "y": 64, "w": 208, "h": 88}}, "edges": {"invalidate": "M234 86 L274 86", "rows": "M486 86 L526 86"}, "labels": []}, "narrow": {"size": [320, 500], "nodes": {"table": {"x": 40, "y": 26, "w": 240, "h": 88}, "query": {"x": 40, "y": 182, "w": 240, "h": 88}, "ui": {"x": 40, "y": 338, "w": 240, "h": 88}}, "edges": {"invalidate": "M120 116 L120 180", "rows": "M120 272 L120 336"}, "labels": [], "pk": {"dx": 10, "dy": 5, "anchor": "start"}}}, "modes": {"run": {"initial": {"nodes": {"table": ["", "Ana, Ben"], "query": ["", "observing users"], "ui": ["", "collecting"]}}, "steps": [{"caption": "A collector starts the users query. In this run its first result contains Ana and Ben.", "packets": [{"edge": "rows", "label": "initial rows", "tone": "fwd"}], "set": {"nodes": {"ui": ["is-done", "[Ana, Ben]"]}}}, {"caption": "A repository inserts Chen and commits. The stored table changes; the old result in the collector does not update itself.", "set": {"nodes": {"table": ["is-active", "Ana, Ben, Chen"]}}}, {"caption": "The users-table invalidation wakes the observable query, which reads the database again. The signal says that the table changed; it does not carry the new row list.", "packets": [{"edge": "invalidate", "label": "invalidate", "tone": "fwd"}], "set": {"nodes": {"query": ["is-active", "re-querying"]}}}, {"caption": "The new query result reaches the collector. Invalidation is per table, so even a write outside a query’s result can cause a re-query; distinctUntilChanged can suppress equal downstream results.", "packets": [{"edge": "rows", "label": "fresh rows", "tone": "fwd"}], "set": {"nodes": {"query": ["is-done", "read complete"], "ui": ["is-done", "[Ana, Ben, Chen]"]}}}, {"caption": "A write only to playlists does not invalidate this users-only query. No users invalidation or row packet moves.", "set": {"nodes": {"table": ["", "unchanged users"], "query": ["", "observing users"]}}}, {"caption": "Cancelling collection ends this query’s observation. Later writes have no delivery path to this cancelled collector.", "set": {"nodes": {"query": ["", "observation ended"], "ui": ["", "cancelled"]}}}]}}}</script>
<p class="pb-sub">Sources: <a href="https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/room/async-queries">Room asynchronous queries</a>.</p>
</section>

<!-- @diagram b33f8a4b14376953 -->
### Where Room sits in the data flow

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-stack"><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node"><strong>Compose UI</strong><small>observes <code>StateFlow</code></small></div><div class="node"><strong>ViewModel</strong><small>observes the repository's <code>Flow</code></small></div></div><div class="down"></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>Repository</strong><small>queries Room as a <code>Flow</code>; inserts what the network returns</small></div><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node" data-state="done"><strong>Room database</strong><small>source of truth; its InvalidationTracker re-triggers queries</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Retrofit network</strong><small>syncs into the repository, never straight to the UI</small></div></div></div><figcaption>The network writes; Room notifies; the UI reads. Each arrow has one direction.</figcaption></figure>

